WEBVTT

00:00:00.065 --> 00:00:01.836
Which number belongs first?

00:00:02.227 --> 00:00:02.669
One.

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:06.810
But how could a program find every next number without searching

00:00:06.823 --> 00:00:07.904
the whole row again?

00:00:08.724 --> 00:00:10.795
Start with two smaller problems.

00:00:11.198 --> 00:00:12.514
Split the row in half.

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:14.727
Nothing has changed order yet.

00:00:15.528 --> 00:00:17.130
Split each half again.

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.994
Now we only need to put a pair of numbers in order.

00:00:20.824 --> 00:00:22.270
Split once more.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:25.226
A number on its own is already sorted.

00:00:25.629 --> 00:00:27.101
Now we can build back up.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:29.148
Three beats seven.

00:00:29.565 --> 00:00:30.763
Two beats eight.

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:34.188
On each side, copy the smaller number first.

00:00:34.591 --> 00:00:35.880
Then let the other follow.

00:00:36.708 --> 00:00:39.260
Put each finished pair back where it belongs.

00:00:39.637 --> 00:00:42.164
We have four little rows that are already in order.

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:46.168
Here, two beats three, while one beats four.

00:00:46.533 --> 00:00:48.160
Then compare the next fronts.

00:00:48.551 --> 00:00:50.582
Only the side we took from moves forward.

00:00:51.382 --> 00:00:52.528
Each half is ready.

00:00:52.918 --> 00:00:55.926
The numbers inside it are ordered, but the whole row still

00:00:55.939 --> 00:00:56.720
needs joining.

00:00:57.519 --> 00:01:00.409
Now watch: one, then two, then three.

00:01:00.787 --> 00:01:03.521
We only look at the fronts, because nothing behind them

00:01:03.521 --> 00:01:04.420
can be smaller.

00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:07.740
When one side runs out, the rest follows.

00:01:08.541 --> 00:01:10.664
Now put the finished row back.

00:01:11.067 --> 00:01:14.179
Every number has found its place, from one through eight.

00:01:15.011 --> 00:01:16.222
That is merge sort.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:19.894
Make small sorted pieces, then let their fronts guide you

00:01:19.894 --> 00:01:21.288
to a bigger sorted row.
